#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:3 cf7fd6bc0b8f47829555f5e239164c26
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:6 4b67789847734f14bcc18480ce93c9ea
msgid "Qubes OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:8 ef70d20018d54aaf9256c4241450a5b3
msgid ""
"A security-oriented operating system (OS). The main principle of Qubes OS is "
"security by compartmentalization (isolation), in which activities are "
"compartmentalized (isolated) in separate :term:`qubes <qube>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:10 fc7b3764390e413591626abdf9a00005
msgid ""
"**Important:** The official name is \"Qubes OS\" (note the capitalization "
"and the space between \"Qubes\" and \"OS\"). In casual conversation, this is "
"often shortened to \"Qubes\". Only in technical contexts where spaces are "
"not permitted (e.g., in usernames) may the space be omitted, as in "
"``@QubesOS``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:14 26fea1079b0a450b9262bb23c9b824f0
msgid "qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:16 b7cbf592fa2949a38e0caadb87fdf11c
msgid ""
"A secure compartment in Qubes OS. Currently, qubes are implemented as Xen :"
"term:`domains <domain>`, but Qubes OS is independent of its underlying "
"compartmentalization technology. :term:`VMs <VM>` could be replaced with a "
"different technology, and qubes would still be called \"qubes\". Therefore, "
"always opt for the term ``qube`` over the other terms unless explicitly "
"guided otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:18 1506bb353c524010bf2b49e0037e8e3f
msgid ""
"**Important:** The term \"qube\" is a common noun and should follow the "
"capitalization rules of common nouns. For example, \"I have three qubes\" is "
"correct, while \"I have three Qubes\" is incorrect. Note that starting a "
"sentence with the plural of \"qube\" (i.e., \"Qubes ...\") can be ambiguous, "
"since it may not be clear whether the referent is a plurality of qubes or :"
"term:`Qubes OS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:20 35420b852ea548b6913ea3fa2f8b5597
msgid ""
"Example usage: Bank in your ``banking`` qube and web surf in your "
"``untrusted`` qube. That way, if your ``untrusted`` qube is compromised, "
"your banking activities remains secure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:22 65505540de94431b8d31d008495a7cda
msgid ""
"Historical note: The term \"qube\" was originally invented as an alternative "
"to \"VM\", and was intended to make it easier for less technical users to "
"understand Qubes OS and learn how to use it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:23 4bf5f218a55a40bf92e9bcf3cb388b85
msgid "domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:25 52086592f9ca488e8b19f7f97fb90ddf
msgid ""
"In Xen, a synonym for a virtual machine. See `\"domain\" on the Xen Wiki "
"<https://wiki.xenproject.org/wiki/Domain>`__. This term has no official "
"meaning in Qubes OS, but is often used colloquially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:26 00a53a43ec124563a117c1944cdac24c
msgid "VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:28 2ce60bbf5d534622a8954aae90ef1837
msgid ""
"An abbreviation for \"virtual machine\". A software implementation of a "
"computer that provides the functionality of a physical machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:31 f92e47d8b4f044089a5ee0f771262141
msgid "Qube types and properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:35 d0d3ae07339443f7988a7be89eb8b0a7
msgid "admin qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:41 46c0db836422448da365c238769378eb
msgid ""
"A type of :term:`qube` used for administering Qubes OS. In the default "
"install, the only admin qube is :term:`dom0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:42 6af68b44ad684f6d87aa1434342bcf78
msgid "app qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:48 c10386bec3674f72be7e25999bdb9a73
msgid ""
"A :term:`qube` that is based on a template. Normally, *app qubes* are used "
"to run user applications and store user files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:50 cd6c2c01b619406482725e5a09a6617c
msgid ""
"An *app qube* does not have a root file system of its own. The qube borrows "
"its root file system from its  :term:`template`, and only owns its own home "
"directory and user files. (In Linux-based qubes, these are the :file:`/home` "
"and :file:`/usr/local` directories.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:52 335a8079dfc8460eb36bb4383eeca32d
msgid "Previously known as: ``AppVM``, ``TemplateBasedVM``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:54 d3e43d747d674ae38d2a5793a23b70c0
msgid "disposable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:60 2dcb289f94b44940869c4c0fb4b7d7fd
msgid ""
"A :term:`disposable` qube is a stateless :term:`qube` - it does not save any "
"data between reboots. Every time it is started, it has the same fresh file "
"system.  These qubes can be used for a variety of situations, from "
"experimentation to creating a more secure network connection. See :doc:`/"
"user/how-to-guides/how-to-use-disposables`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:62 20ab9cff549b4f16aa9f0feb8b590816
msgid ""
"Typically, disposable qubes have a temporary name (**dispXYZ**, where XYZ is "
"a random number). They cease to exist after the qube is shut down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:64 fb1f5a7bdbe747588c426ab41d0d1fb4
msgid ""
"Closing the **first** application that was opened in the disposable will "
"trigger the qube to shut down. If you have opened a second application that "
"will be closed. You will lose any data unless you have copied it out of the "
"disposable: this is done automatically if you have chosen to ``edit in "
"disposable`` and have saved any changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:66 f2ccfb9bc7a94bfa9ee5e939dfeae65d
msgid ""
"Multiple instances of a disposable qube based on a single disposable "
"template can run at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:68 6bce637069d1458bb06db70c632959d9
msgid "See also :term:`named disposable`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:70 d857cb109efd43e181526da20a9664e9
msgid "Previously known as: ``DisposableVM``, ``DispVM``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:71 8f80c46ab85242ceac0c556a527950c2
msgid "standalone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:77 d6e66c8169e145de9232a7e078aa7771
msgid ""
"Any :term:`qube` that has its own root file system and does not share it "
"with another qube. (It is **not** based on a template and it is **not** a "
"template itself.) Distinct from both :term:`template` and :term:`app qube`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:79
#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:177 2a4d77bc00384bd0ba62af056fe68cc0
#: 998291d30c84422f8c80c7f89eefc19b
msgid "See :doc:`/user/advanced-topics/standalones-and-hvms`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:81 8eb0a95e9d244664a8dcc945acd8ba70
msgid "Previously known as: ``StandaloneVM``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:82 ebddb8bdc09f48ab9181caedb549f257
msgid "template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:88 bd163fe5cfef43f491892c4981b8df04
msgid ""
"Any :term:`qube` that provides its root file system to other qube(s). A qube "
"that is borrowing a template's root file system is known as an :term:`app "
"qube` and is said to be \"based on\" the template. Templates are intended "
"for installing and updating software applications, but not for running them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:90 909eee2dea5149468a0bee22d5a3d28f
msgid "See :doc:`/user/templates/templates`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:92 01aca872f5db457aaca2c3e0b5e6db2c
msgid "No template is an :term:`app qube`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:94 c45caa522f2144438165b6b298b103b3
msgid "A template cannot be based on another template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:96 f4be143045834ac6af4a9f59e380bf40
msgid ""
"Regular templates cannot function as :term:`disposable template`. "
"(Disposable templates must be app qubes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:98 013f101f47ce469fa6f4fb126997e5c6
msgid "Previously known as: ``TemplateVM``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:99 dec4e97d229f4c13abc5d5a3edeea839
msgid "disposable template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:105 51534ae76a354739a5db7d9bd6e739ba
msgid ""
"Any :term:`app qube` on which :term:`disposables <disposable>` are based. A "
"disposable template shares its user directories (and, indirectly, the root "
"file system of the regular :term:`template` on which it is based) with all :"
"term:`disposable` qubes based on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:107 6543f82bb9c74770b68830df5ad339b1
msgid ""
"Not to be confused with the concept of a regular :term:`template` that is "
"itself disposable - this is not a possible configuration in Qubes OS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:109 2540460f9d52481d9a5c114c287f9ac9
msgid ""
"Disposable templates must be app qubes. They cannot be regular :term:"
"`templates <template>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:111 bb17075a3d7241a6808eb927e864698d
msgid ""
"Every :term:`disposable` is based on a disposable template, which is in turn "
"based on a regular :term:`template`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:113 ae16492f6ca24e949da756c29c4573d0
msgid ""
"Unlike :term:`disposables <disposable>`, disposable templates behave like "
"normal :term:`app qubes <app qube>` in terms of persistence - their contents "
"survive reboots. Thus, you can configure your disposable template to have e."
"g. browser extensions or configuration that will be present in every "
"disposable qube based on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:115 3bab64ea17eb475591bb6156dc222f1c
msgid ""
"Previously known as: ``DisposableVM Template``, ``DVM Template``, ``DVM``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:116 e199b205b84a4cd096828e0406e58d58
msgid "named disposable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:122 c64eb934e98941e49428fcad151f5df1
msgid ""
"A type of :term:`disposable` given a permanent name. This qube continues to "
"exist even after it is shut down and can be started again. Unlike normal "
"disposable qubes, it is also not tied to the program it was started with and "
"will not shut down when the program closes. In all other respects, it "
"behaves like a disposable qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:124 31c6313311d847c083369f5f17d6aa9f
msgid "Only one instance of a named disposable can run at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:126 0fe211a4faa6439cb5db8238600e71ad
msgid ""
"Technical note: Named disposables are useful for certain :term:`service "
"qube`\\ s, where the combination of persistent device assignment and "
"ephemeral qube state is desirable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:127 47208d31029b4c0b866c2f7bae04f12b
msgid "management qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:129 bec1bd6bb7a44c38818e58596015481b
msgid ""
"A :term:`qube` used for automated management of a Qubes OS installation via :"
"doc:`/user/advanced-topics/salt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:130 80a95a190bd0418c86d080556e42e059
msgid "net qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:132 305dc3c3ae1b43209e338f37d774822a
msgid ""
"A property of any qube that tells the system which (if any) :term:`service "
"qube` to use to connect to the network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:134 f34ed97bf8724b06afcfcd7a78e59130
msgid ""
"If a qube does not have a net qube (i.e., its ``net qube`` is set to "
"``None`` in qube settings), then that qube is offline. It is disconnected "
"from all networking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:136 2389bf8f35544537b8ce978630e7a248
msgid "Internally, this property is named as `netvm`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:137 0c38ff05d5bd4287b48b7c72c61eded8
msgid "service qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:143 355258e3f25f45749dd4d740b545cdc6
msgid ""
"Any :term:`app qube` with the primary purpose of providing services to other "
"qubes. ``sys-net`` and ``sys-firewall`` are examples of service qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:144 77c3dc876c3542c2bae62c48c13884ed
msgid "internal qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:146 0b7ccb863d4d445c9f990b688cc21724
msgid ""
"A qube which has the ``internal`` feature set. Those qubes are hidden from "
"GUI tools such as user menu and have many GUI features disabled. They are "
"used for the :term:`management qube` and preloading disposable qubes. In "
"most cases, internal qubes should not be manipulated by the user directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:147 c96ae9e26a734a6e84eccbb031f28182
msgid "interface qube"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:149 0c29bb57884a40baaede11c36fbbdb71
msgid ""
"An interface qube handles display-related tasks and some system management. "
"There can be more than one interface qube present on the system. Each "
"interface qube can have its own set of privileges, permissions, managed "
"qubes, etc. In the initial install, :term:`dom0` is the only interface qube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:151 dcdf6a63a6754487bbc602d0049cd088
msgid "Previously known as: ``GuiVM``, ``GUI domain``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:152 e4805a1ad431429b9e5a22706cdfc0ce
msgid "GUI domain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:154 640a1a5fe5464d978309ae221e3629dc
msgid "Outdated term for :term:`interface qube`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:157 d62213c2fb524bbba91b728bfebd88df
msgid "Other terms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:161 653261ca45e145f5821d06f767326a03
msgid "dom0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:163 c31b77b40a144b5bbb215ee06d92458b
msgid ""
"A type of :term:`admin qube`. Also known as the **host** :term:`domain`, "
"dom0 is the initial qube started by the Xen hypervisor on boot. Dom0 runs "
"the Xen management toolstack and has special privileges relative to other "
"domains, such as direct access to most hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:165 1f6f5f4d5bf24ed9a62490c3b5948a03
msgid ""
"The term \"dom0\" is a common noun and should follow the capitalization "
"rules of common nouns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:166 e403787713204b188bdde4f310034b7d
msgid "domU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:168 08212eff59f94305bc955a5862f7c167
msgid ""
"Unprivileged :term:`domain`. Also known as **guest** domains, domUs are the "
"counterparts to dom0. In Xen, all VMs except dom0 are domUs. By default, "
"most domUs lack direct hardware access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:170 b91415c754214dee8f362ab7954c5377
msgid ""
"The term \"domU\" is a common noun and should follow the capitalization "
"rules of common nouns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:172 861e6ed9d01348b583289fe7831f5610
msgid ""
"Sometimes the term :term:`vm` is used as a synonym for domU. This is "
"technically inaccurate, as :term:`dom0` is also a VM in Xen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:173 a348a4d845bd484d9e057b47ec4986be
msgid "HVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:175 b763a10ea2564623a0f5ca2d5990bb3f
msgid ""
"Hardware-assisted Virtual Machine. Any fully virtualized, or hardware-"
"assisted, :term:`qube` utilizing the virtualization extensions of the host "
"CPU. Although HVMs are typically slower than paravirtualized qubes due to "
"the required emulation, HVMs allow the user to create domains based on any "
"operating system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:178 9c587633fafd4c6e94c1cef6c8f8e9b8
msgid "firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:180 ac2af7bb113248659edcb45036e804d8
msgid ""
"Software that runs outside the control of the operating system. Some "
"firmware executes on the same CPU cores as Qubes OS does, but all computers "
"have many additional processors that the operating system does not run on, "
"and these processors also run firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:181 5c28360b038648bc9c378af9323ec8b0
msgid "policies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:183 97f7ef61ef7a49a8860337ccfbb2b122
msgid ""
"In Qubes OS, \"policies\" govern interactions between qubes, powered by :doc:"
"`Qubes' qrexec system </developer/services/qrexec>`. A single policy is a "
"rule applied to a qube or set of qubes, that governs how and when "
"information or assets may be shared with other qubes. An example is the "
"rules governing how files can be copied between qubes. Policy rules are "
"grouped together in files under ``/etc/qubes/policy.d`` Policies are an "
"important part of what makes Qubes OS special."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:187 cac5eaba84634e87bb9dd8186d34995e
msgid "Qubes Windows Tools (QWT)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:189 2e7939e77a894f05b4d812066929ac9c
msgid ""
"A set of programs and drivers that provide integration of Windows qubes with "
"the rest of the Qubes OS system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/reference/glossary.rst:191 f939fcd4a54d43d1b2683dd09d78d5a3
msgid ""
"See :doc:`/user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools` and :doc:`/user/"
"templates/windows/qubes-windows`."
msgstr ""
